  "notes": "{不思議|ふしぎ} functions as both a na-adjective (strange, mysterious) and a noun (wonder, mystery).\n\nFORMS:\n- Na-adjective: {不思議|ふしぎ}な + noun\n- Adverbial: {不思議|ふしぎ}に\n- Noun: {不思議|ふしぎ}\n\nCOMMON EXPRESSIONS:\n- {不思議|ふしぎ}な⟦こと→こと：01164_koto⟧⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧: strangely enough\n- {不思議|ふしぎ}に⟦{思|おも}う→思う：00492_omou⟧: to find strange\n- {不思議|ふしぎ}な⟦{気持|きも}ち→気持ち：01385_kimochi⟧: a strange feeling\n- ⟦{七|なな}→七：00734_nana⟧{不思議|ふしぎ}: seven wonders/mysteries\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {不思議|ふしぎ}な⟦{力|ちから}→力：01661_chikara⟧: mysterious power\n- {不思議|ふしぎ}な⟦{現象|げんしょう}→現象：02718_genshou⟧: strange phenomenon\n- ⟦{自然|しぜん}→自然：01423_shizen⟧⟦の→の：09472_no⟧{不思議|ふしぎ}: wonders of nature\n\nCULTURAL NOTE:\n{不思議|ふしぎ}⟦の→の：09472_no⟧⟦{国|くに}→国：02204_kuni⟧⟦の→の：09472_no⟧アリス = \"Alice in Wonderland\"\n\nThe word conveys a sense of puzzlement or wonder at something beyond ordinary understanding.",
